From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ted Meyer <tmathmeyer@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 13:54:24 -0700
Subject: [Media] Propagate data origin to MultiBufferDataSource

There are a few ways that a URL can change between request and response,
including redirects and service worker interceptions.
GetUrlAfterRedirects only handles cases where the original request is
redirected server-side by a header & status code. If a worker intercepts
the request and replaces it with a response from either somewhere else
or synthetically creates one, that information can also be useful for
making security decisions. It wasn't being propagated, so this CL adds a
way for that to happen, and a use case for it in HLS.

Bug: 543082212
Change-Id: I41b3dd73f23fa2d2211dcd3f37b1e7b83e36b250
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8342168
Reviewed-by: Dale Curtis <dalecurtis@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Ted (Chromium) Meyer <tmathmeyer@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1691072}

Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y):
Picked as a prerequisite of 7628505b506f / fb2af07952f5 / a4a389ea3bf0
(UrlData::data_origin()). The HLS data source provider on this branch does
not have the TrackOrigin()/SetPostRedirectUri() block, so the
hls_data_source_provider_impl.cc hunk and the HLS test helper / unit test
changes were not carried; url_index.h keeps its security_origin() accessor.

